                title: 'Shape',
                subtitle: 'there is literally a square and a triangle and it looks like not a square and a triangle what',
                banner: true,
                image: 'images/thumbnails/shape.png',
                detail: `<h2>Everything is just a bunch a shapes that are molded and glued together to make stuff.</h2><br>
                Both literally and in design, this is true. Atoms have a shape, and they make up your arm, which is a shape, which is a part of you. And guess what,
                you're a lot of shapes. Same goes for design. When drawing a person, you draw the shapes, then you change those shapes to be more arm, and <i>then</i>
                you draw the arm. Drawing the arm from scratch is just gonna lead to proportion issues later on.<br>
                Another cool thing you can do with shapes is make 2D look 3D. For example, this cube is literally just a bunch of bent squares put together:<br><br>
                <img src='images/shapes.gif'>`
